00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:10.520
So what is GDPR?

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:12.900
GDPR is a regulation
that protects

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:17.660
personal data of EU
citizens and the processing

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:19.770
and movement of data as well.

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:24.020
So this regulation actually goes
into force 25 May of this year.

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:27.710
As you might remember, from
the 23rd onwards of May,

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:29.840
there was many companies
sending you emails

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:32.810
with enhanced [INAUDIBLE]
conditions requesting

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:37.460
your consent to use your data
for their processing needs.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:42.050
Now that's the first step to
GDPR is obtaining consent.

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:43.700
Who does this affect?

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:46.610
This affects any organization
that collects, stores,

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:49.070
and processes personal data.

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:51.600
And this is on
European citizens.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.780
So it doesn't matter if
you are from a US company

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.370
or you are an Asian company.

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:58.430
You will have to comply with
these regulations as well.

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:03.380
And any noncompliance actually
comes with a very huge fine.

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:09.229
The fine can come to almost
a 4% of the annual revenue.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:11.110
Now let's talk
about personal data.

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:13.210
So these are some
examples of personal data.

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:16.250
Things like your
name, your ID number,

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:18.987
or in the US, your
Social Security number,

00:02:18.987 --> 00:02:20.820
your credit card number,
your email address.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:25.110
Even your picture is
data that belongs to you.

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:27.010
Now you can see
it in many forms.

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:29.227
You can see it as structured
data in the database.

00:02:29.227 --> 00:02:30.810
Or you can see it
as unstructured data

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:34.620
in your Google Docs, your
slides, or your spreadsheets,

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:37.640
and even in emails.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:40.080
Think about it this way--

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:43.954
data, as we know it now
in GDPR, the companies

00:02:43.954 --> 00:02:45.120
don't own your data anymore.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:46.536
What you're doing,
you're actually

00:02:46.536 --> 00:02:49.650
loaning your data to the
companies for them to use it.

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:51.630
And you have the
right to control

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:53.100
that data which you give them.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:56.010
So this is what GDPR is about.

00:02:56.010 --> 00:03:00.110
So what are the main protections
given by GDPR to EU citizens?

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:02.730
I'd like to use a
