00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:49.480
And what the DevOps
guys can go in to do,

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:51.479
actually, is just tag it
as benign or malicious.

00:08:51.479 --> 00:08:55.800
It's a very simple,
continuously-improving process.

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:57.830
So for example, let's
just type in some

00:08:57.830 --> 00:08:59.690
addresses here to classify.

00:08:59.690 --> 00:09:03.550
So you'd look at
google.com, for example.

00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:07.110
There's a very low chance
of being malicious.

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:09.114
Let's take a long
address domain name just

00:09:09.114 --> 00:09:11.280
to check [INAUDIBLE] length
